Manuscript and supplementary figures generated from the processed repository data.

### `stability_figures/`

LHS stability, identifiability and calibration sensitivity figures.

## Interpretation of retained distributions

The calibration procedure retains parameter combinations satisfying specified 
biological and epidemiological criteria. The resulting distributions are 
therefore referred to as **retained parameter distributions**.

They are not Bayesian posterior distributions.

Similarly, reported 2.5th–97.5th percentile intervals describe the distributions 
of retained parameter values or model outcomes and should not be interpreted as 
Bayesian credible intervals.
